### NOTE (side effect, found after the run): the script was meant to leave the measured repo untouched. It created no objects and
### changed no content, index or refs there, but git "freshens" objects that already exist, even through an alternate object
### directory: 11 loose objects and one pack file in "~/Projects/Hermes Agent Auto/.git/objects" had their mtime set to the run time
### (their birth times are all 2026-08-27; see B10-side-effect.txt). Nothing was reverted, to avoid a second write to that repo.
